\begin{enumerate}
\item All the things in the world are similar/different.
\item Some things are the same/similar to each other.
\end{enumerate}

Let \( x = 10 \) and \( y = 5 \). Find the value of each of the following expressions:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( x - y = \_\_\_ \) (1 mark)
\item \( 3x + 2y = \_\_\_ \) (1 mark)
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( x - y = 10 - 5 = 5 \)
\item \( 3x + 2y = 3(10) + 2(5) = 30 + 10 = 40 \)
\end{enumerate}

\paragraph{Investigation} Slowing down toy cars
\begin{enumerate}
\item Collect a toy car that moves.
\item Find a flat surface to use as a track.
\item Work with a partner to explore how you can slow down the car.
\item Write or draw your results in your Investigation Notebook.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Toy cars
\item A flat surface to use as a track
\end{itemize}

